course: dictionary
lesson: 8405
title: Sound words and hidden meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rumbling means a long, deep, low sound, like thunder far away or a big truck passing. Sound words help you hear a story. «Alice hears a rumbling of little cartwheels and many voices» tells you the sound is low and far off, like wheels and a crowd moving together.
explain: Rumbling can also be a feeling inside your body. A rumbling tummy means your stomach is making a low sound because you are hungry. The word is still about a low sound, but this time it comes from inside you.
explain: Rumblings, in the plural, can mean early signs that trouble is coming. A town might have rumblings of trouble before anything has actually happened. Look at the words around the word to choose the right meaning.
fact: Rumbling means making a long, deep, low sound.
fact: Thunder far away, or a big truck passing, can make a rumbling sound.
fact: A rumbling tummy is the sound your stomach makes when you are hungry.
fact: Rumblings are early signs that people are unhappy or that trouble is coming.
fact: In science, a rumbling is a low-pitched sound made by slow vibrations.
exercise: In «Alice hears a rumbling of little cartwheels and many voices», what is the rumbling? | *A long, low, distant sound | A sudden sharp shout | A bright flash of light | A gentle breeze
exercise: Sam's tummy is rumbling before lunch. What is it telling him? | He has lost his bag | *He is hungry | He is tired of school | He is cold
exercise: The newspaper spoke of rumblings of trouble in the town. What are the rumblings here? | Flowers opening early | Loud music from a band | *Early signs that trouble may be coming | Very large stones
test: Which thing can make a rumbling sound? | A tiny ant | A soft whisper | A bright light | *Thunder far away
test: The story spoke of rumblings before the volcano erupted. What do rumblings suggest here? | A happy birthday party | *Early signs of danger coming | A new pair of shoes | Calm and quiet weather
exam: The mountain began to rumble, and the villagers felt a cold fear. What do the rumbles warn of? | *Danger may be coming from the mountain | A trip to the beach | Dinner is ready | A visit from a friend
